<span id="important">
  <h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="changes">Version 2.0 changes</h2>
</span>

<p class="govuk-body">
  Released Monday 12 October 2026
</p>

<h3 class="govuk-heading-m">
  Pagination required
</h3>

<p class="govuk-body">
  When retrieving applications, pagination is required. The <code>page</code> and <code>per_page</code> parameters allow you to handle large volumes of applications in smaller, manageable batches.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
  Use the <code>page</code> parameter to retrieve the indicated page of results. The first call should ask for page 1. Use the <code>links</code> object in the response to navigate subsequent paginated results.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
  Use the <code>per_page</code> parameter to specify how many applications to return per page. This is optional and defaults to 50, which is also the maximum value.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
  This is the only breaking change coming with v2.0.
</p>
